{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Current Gap\n\nStories 1934, 749c, 1fd4, and 0b14 landed authenticated `undeclared`, `paths`, and `none` behavior. The current packaged author guide mentions only the paths form at `src/rebar/_guides/writing-a-passing-plan.md:96-100`; `docs/event-schema.md:52` still describes FILE_IMPACT only as a path/reason array. The standalone gate and ticket-model docs likewise lack one complete author-facing tri-state contract. This ticket creates that missing documentation. Because it edits repository files, its own scope is `paths`, never `none`.\n\n## Approach\n\nDocument one already-landed contract at four reader-facing locations and behavior-test the only location exposed through a runtime public entry point: `rebar explain plan`. Verify the three standalone docs with a durable, auditable semantic checklist rather than source-grep or snapshot tests. The runtime test intentionally cannot prove, or make pass, any standalone-doc criterion; completion requires both the green public behavior test and the separate evidence-bearing checklist. Rejected alternative: tests that open documentation source files and search for mandated wording, because those are change detectors coupled to text placement rather than public behavior.\n\n## Authoritative Landed Semantics\n\n`src/rebar/reducer/_processors.py:527-543` is the implementation evidence. Every later FILE_IMPACT event replaces all three derived fields:\n\n- `paths`: a non-empty `file_impact` list, `file_impact_scope=\"paths\"`, and `no_file_impact_reason=\"\"`.\n- `none`: `file_impact=[]`, `file_impact_scope=\"none\"`, and the supplied substantive `no_file_impact_reason`.\n- `undeclared`: `file_impact=[]`, `file_impact_scope=\"undeclared\"`, and `no_file_impact_reason=\"\"`.\n\nThus transition to paths clears any none reason; transition to none clears prior paths; transition to undeclared clears both paths and reason.\n\n## Authoritative Review Criterion\n\nThe advisory `no-file-impact` plan-review criterion is registered at `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/registry.py:171-173`, specified at `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/criteria_routing.json:286-309`, and prompted by `src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_no-file-impact.md`. It applies only when `file_impact_scope == \"none\"`, has advisory default posture and a 0.95 block threshold, and asks three sub-answers: whether the declaration is plausible for the deliverable, whether the reason concretely explains why no repository artifact is needed, and whether the plan itself names a repository edit. The author guide will describe this as advisory LLM review, not as a guaranteed claim blocker. The story additionally requires a useful reason to say where non-repository output or evidence lives.\n\n## Execution Steps\n\n1. Update `docs/plan-review-gate.md` with an explicit tri-state section: state freshness, live-child neutral/poison roll-up, closed-child exclusion, material-fingerprint effects, and a mixed paths-plus-none example.\n2. Update `docs/ticket-model.md` beside file impact with the three persisted states and the rule that docs-only/test-only repository changes declare paths.\n3. Update `docs/event-schema.md` FILE_IMPACT wording with the three event fields and the exact replacement/clearing semantics above.\n4. Update `src/rebar/_guides/writing-a-passing-plan.md`, packaged source for public `rebar explain plan`. Give a separable author contract: the three choices; `rebar set-file-impact <id> --none \"<reason>\"`; no repository file changes; docs-only/test-only use paths; the advisory LLM criterion; and a reason explaining both `Why no repository files change` and `Where output or evidence lives`. Include one valid worked reason.\n5. RED-first, add `test_explain_plan_file_impact_tristate_contract` in `tests/unit/test_plan_review_explain.py`. Invoke public `main([\"explain\", \"plan\"])`, assert exit code 0, and capture stdout. Case-normalized presence assertions check these stable public markers without order or layout dependence: `undeclared`, `paths`, `none`, `set-file-impact`, `--none`, `no repository file`, `docs-only`, `test-only`, `advisory`, `no-file-impact`, `why no repository files change`, and `where output or evidence lives`. Also assert the pre-existing `rebar review-plan` marker remains as a negative control against replacing the guide wholesale. This test must not open or grep source files, inspect private implementation shape, snapshot exact prose, or assert formatting/order.\n6. Before the guide edit, run the new test and confirm it fails because the current public command omits the none command and author guidance, proving the discoverability gap through the real entry point. After the guide edit, rerun green. For the teeth check, temporarily remove the newly documented public tri-state block, confirm the same public test fails, restore it, and confirm green. Moving or reheading unchanged guidance must leave the test green.\n7. Manually verify standalone criteria GATE-1 through EVENT-2 below. Record one Markdown table as a ticket comment with columns `criterion`, `PASS/FAIL`, `path:line`, and `semantic evidence`, plus reviewer identity, UTC timestamp, and tested git commit SHA. Each row quotes or faithfully paraphrases the passage. Use this template: `| GATE-1 | PASS | docs/plan-review-gate.md:line | undeclared binds whole HEAD |`. Audit with `rebar show cf33-642c-4984-4a87 --output llm` and `git show <recorded-sha>:<recorded-path>`. Any missing or FAIL row blocks completion.\n8. Add a CONSISTENCY row to the same comment with path:line evidence from all four sources. Mark PASS only when the meanings of undeclared, paths, and none agree. This reconciliation is separate from the CLI test.\n9. Run `make lint`, the project typecheck gate, and the full test suite.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n### Standalone documentation\n\n- [ ] GATE-1: `docs/plan-review-gate.md` defines undeclared as whole-HEAD freshness; verified by its PASS checklist row with path:line semantic evidence.\n- [ ] GATE-2: the gate doc defines paths as dependency-scoped freshness; verified by its PASS checklist row.\n- [ ] GATE-3: the gate doc defines authenticated none as contributing no file dependencies; verified by its PASS checklist row.\n- [ ] GATE-4: the gate doc states a live none child is neutral in container roll-up; verified by its PASS checklist row.\n- [ ] GATE-5: the gate doc states a live undeclared child poisons inheritance; verified by its PASS checklist row.\n- [ ] GATE-6: the gate doc states a closed child is excluded from roll-up; verified by its PASS checklist row.\n- [ ] GATE-7: the gate doc states changing a declaration changes the material fingerprint; verified by its PASS checklist row.\n- [ ] GATE-8: the gate doc gives a mixed example where a paths child contributes dependencies and a none child does not; verified by its PASS checklist row.\n- [ ] MODEL-1: `docs/ticket-model.md` documents all three persisted states beside file impact; verified by its PASS checklist row.\n- [ ] MODEL-2: the ticket-model doc states docs-only work uses paths; verified by its PASS checklist row.\n- [ ] MODEL-3: the ticket-model doc states test-only work uses paths; verified by its PASS checklist row.\n- [ ] EVENT-1: `docs/event-schema.md` documents `file_impact`, `file_impact_scope`, and `no_file_impact_reason`; verified by its PASS checklist row.\n- [ ] EVENT-2: the event-schema doc documents replacement and clearing semantics for every target state; verified by its PASS checklist row.\n\n### Public CLI behavior\n\n- [ ] CLI-1: public `rebar explain plan` succeeds and communicates undeclared, paths, and none; verified by `test_explain_plan_file_impact_tristate_contract`.\n- [ ] CLI-2: public output communicates the none command; verified by the public CLI test.\n- [ ] CLI-3: public output communicates that none means no repository file is touched; verified by the public CLI test.\n- [ ] CLI-4: public output communicates that docs-only work uses paths; verified by the public CLI test.\n- [ ] CLI-5: public output communicates that test-only work uses paths; verified by the public CLI test.\n- [ ] CLI-6: public output identifies the no-file-impact check as advisory LLM review; verified by the public CLI test.\n- [ ] CLI-7: public output separately communicates why no repository files change; verified by the public CLI test.\n- [ ] CLI-8: public output separately communicates where output or evidence lives; verified by the public CLI test.\n\n### Completion evidence\n\n- [ ] EVIDENCE-1: the ticket comment contains PASS rows for every GATE, MODEL, EVENT, and CONSISTENCY item with path:line evidence, reviewer, UTC timestamp, and commit SHA; audited with the commands in step 7.\n- [ ] EVIDENCE-2: RED, GREEN, defect-seeded mutation RED, and restored GREEN results for the public CLI behavior test are recorded on the ticket.\n- [ ] QUALITY-1: no automated test reads or greps documentation source, asserts private shape, snapshots exact prose, or depends on formatting/order; verified by code review of the test diff.\n- [ ] SCOPE-1: no production logic or schema file changes; under `src/rebar`, only `_guides/writing-a-passing-plan.md` changes; verified by `git diff --name-only origin/main...HEAD`.\n- [ ] GATE-LINT: `make lint` passes.\n- [ ] GATE-TYPE: the project typecheck gate passes.\n- [ ] GATE-TEST: the full test suite passes."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785263510084080001,"uuid":"fb8958d2-4eff-4cce-a18a-e54dc66a102c"}